  "body": "## Summary\nsUSDM implements ERC-4626 with a non-zero _decimalsOffset() but overrides decimals() to an inconsistent value, causing share-unit mismatches between ERC-4626 math and what integrators/users think the share token decimals are. This can lead to incorrect pricing/quotes, wrong UI display, and unsafe integration behavior for any system relying on ERC-4626 semantics.\n\n## Affected code\n1. src/tokens/sUSDM.sol\n- _decimalsOffset() returns 6\n- decimals() is overridden to return 6\n\nUnder OpenZeppelin ERC-4626, the vault’s decimals should be:\nvaultDecimals=assetDecimals+_decimalsOffset()\nUSDM uses 6 decimals, so with _decimalsOffset() = 6, ERC-4626 expects sUSDM.decimals() to be 12.\n\n## Issue details\nIn OZ ERC-4626 v5.x, the conversion functions rely on _decimalsOffset():\n\n- _convertToShares uses totalSupply() + 10**_decimalsOffset()\n- _convertToAssets uses totalSupply() + 10**_decimalsOffset()\nSo the contract’s internal accounting is explicitly configured for a +6 decimals offset (virtual shares model), but at the same time the token reports only 6 decimals via decimals().\n\nThis creates a semantic inconsistency:\n\n- On-chain ERC-4626 math behaves as though shares have 12-decimal scaling vs the underlying.\n\n- Off-chain and integrator assumptions (wallets, indexers, routers, vault aggregators, price/oracle adapters) will treat shares as 6 decimals and may scale values incorrectly.\n\n## Impact\n1. Incorrect share pricing / quoting: integrators computing price-per-share, exchange rates, or minOut/maxIn using share decimals can produce incorrect values.\n\n2. Unsafe integration behavior: vault routers and aggregators may pass wrongly-scaled amounts (especially in systems that normalize to 18 or to decimals()), potentially causing:\n- deposits/mints failing unexpectedly,\n- wrong slippage protections,\n- misleading UI amounts that cause users to sign transactions they don’t intend.\n3. Accounting/reporting drift: dashboards and off-chain accounting that rely on decimals() to format shares can misreport balances and APY.\n\nEven if core protocol flows “work” in isolation, this is a high-severity integration correctness bug for an ERC-4626 share token.\n\n## Proof / reasoning\n1. sUSDM._decimalsOffset() returns 6, enabling the OZ ERC-4626 “virtual shares” mechanism at 10**6.\n\n2. OZ ERC-4626 defines decimals() as underlyingDecimals + _decimalsOffset().\n3. sUSDM.decimals() is overridden to always return 6, contradicting the ERC-4626 implementation assumptions.\n\n## Recommendation\nits better to just choose one consistent model:\n\n1. Option A (recommended): keep the offset, fix decimals()\n\n- Remove the decimals() override and let OZ compute it.\n- Result: sUSDM.decimals() becomes 12 (given USDM has 6 decimals), matching ERC-4626 semantics.\n\n2. Option B: keep decimals() = 6, remove the offset\n\n- Set _decimalsOffset() to 0 (and re-evaluate the intended inflation-attack mitigation / virtual shares configuration).\n- Result: shares and assets both use 6 decimals, and ERC-4626 semantics stay consistent.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\nimport \"../src/tokens/USDM.sol\";\nimport \"../src/tokens/sUSDM.sol\";\nimport \"../src/core/MonetrixConfig.sol\";\nimport \"../src/core/MonetrixVault.sol\";\nimport \"../src/core/InsuranceFund.sol\";\nimport \"../src/governance/MonetrixAccessController.sol\";\nimport {sUSDMEscrow} from \"../src/tokens/sUSDMEscrow.sol\";\n\nimport \"./mocks/MockUSDC.sol\";\n\n/// @notice PoC: `sUSDM` reports 6 decimals but ERC-4626 math is configured with `_decimalsOffset() = 6`.\n///         This makes raw share amounts appear 1e6x larger than expected to any integrator that trusts `decimals()`.\ncontract sUSDMDecimalsMismatchPoC is Test {\n    MockUSDC usdc;\n    USDM usdm;\n    sUSDM susdm;\n    sUSDMEscrow unstakeEscrow;\n    MonetrixConfig config;\n    MonetrixVault vault;\n    InsuranceFund insurance;\n    MonetrixAccessController acl;\n\n    address admin = address(0xAD);\n    address foundation = address(0xF0);\n    address user = address(0x1);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n\n        usdc = new MockUSDC();\n\n        MonetrixAccessController aclImpl = new MonetrixAccessController();\n        acl = MonetrixAccessController(\n            address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(aclImpl), abi.encodeCall(MonetrixAccessController.initialize, (admin))))\n        );\n\n        USDM usdmImpl = new USDM();\n        usdm = USDM(address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(usdmImpl), abi.encodeCall(USDM.initialize, (address(acl))))));\n\n        InsuranceFund insImpl = new InsuranceFund();\n        insurance = InsuranceFund(\n            address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(insImpl), abi.encodeCall(InsuranceFund.initialize, (address(usdc), address(acl)))))\n        );\n\n        MonetrixConfig configImpl = new MonetrixConfig();\n        config = MonetrixConfig(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(configImpl),\n                    abi.encodeCall(MonetrixConfig.initialize, (address(insurance), foundation, address(acl)))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        sUSDM susdmImpl = new sUSDM();\n        susdm = sUSDM(\n            address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(susdmImpl), abi.encodeCall(sUSDM.initialize, (address(usdm), address(config), address(acl)))))\n        );\n\n        MonetrixVault vaultImpl = new MonetrixVault();\n        vault = MonetrixVault(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(vaultImpl),\n                    abi.encodeCall(\n                        MonetrixVault.initialize,\n                        (address(usdc), address(usdm), address(susdm), address(config), address(0x5678), address(acl))\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        acl.grantRole(acl.GOVERNOR(), admin);\n        acl.grantRole(acl.GUARDIAN(), admin);\n        acl.grantRole(acl.OPERATOR(), admin);\n\n        // Bind vault authorities.\n        usdm.setVault(address(vault));\n        susdm.setVault(address(vault));\n\n        // Wire escrow so cooldown flows are enabled (not required for deposit PoC, but matches production wiring).\n        unstakeEscrow = new sUSDMEscrow(address(usdm), address(susdm));\n        susdm.setEscrow(address(unstakeEscrow));\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Fund user with USDC so they can deposit into the vault and receive USDM.\n        usdc.mint(user, 1_000e6);\n    }\n\n    function test_poc_decimalsMismatch_and_1USDMDepositMints1e12RawShares() public {\n        // Expected ERC-4626 decimals with offset: underlying(6) + offset(6) = 12.\n        uint8 underlyingDecimals = 6; // USDM.decimals()\n        uint8 offset = 6;             // sUSDM._decimalsOffset()\n        uint8 expectedSusdmDecimals = underlyingDecimals + offset;\n\n        // Actual value returned by the token.\n        assertEq(susdm.decimals(), 6, \"sUSDM reports 6 decimals\");\n        assertEq(expectedSusdmDecimals, 12, \"ERC-4626 expects 12 decimals when offset=6\");\n        assertTrue(susdm.decimals() != expectedSusdmDecimals, \"decimals mismatch\");\n\n        // Mint 1 USDM directly to the user (Vault is the only USDM minter).\n        // This avoids MonetrixVault's configured `minDepositAmount` constraints.\n        vm.prank(address(vault));\n        usdm.mint(user, 1e6);\n\n        // Stake 1 USDM into sUSDM.\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        usdm.approve(address(susdm), 1e6);\n        uint256 mintedShares = susdm.deposit(1e6, user);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // With OZ ERC-4626 virtual shares and `_decimalsOffset()=6`, the first deposit mints:\n        // shares = assets * 10**offset = 1e6 * 1e6 = 1e12.\n        assertEq(mintedShares, 1e12, \"1 USDM mints 1e12 raw shares when offset=6\");\n\n        // Demonstrate integrator-facing confusion:\n        // - If you trust `sUSDM.decimals() == 6`, 1e12 raw units display as 1,000,000 sUSDM.\n        // - If ERC-4626 decimals were 12 as expected, it displays as 1.0 sUSDM.\n        uint256 displayedUsingReportedDecimals = mintedShares / 1e6;\n        uint256 displayedUsingExpectedDecimals = mintedShares / 1e12;\n\n        assertEq(displayedUsingReportedDecimals, 1_000_000, \"reported-6dp display is 1,000,000 sUSDM\");\n        assertEq(displayedUsingExpectedDecimals, 1, \"expected-12dp display is 1 sUSDM\");\n    }\n}\n```\nTest Output\n```solidity\nRan 1 test for test/sUSDMDecimalsMismatchPoC.t.sol:sUSDMDecimalsMismatchPoC\n[PASS] test_poc_decimalsMismatch_and_1USDMDepositMints1e12RawShares() (gas: 173047)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 2.06ms (227.80µs CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 11.73ms (2.06ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
